gotten all about those enormous catacombs. So that city came quite high on my list now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1159-kjetilkverndokken","name":"kjetilkverndokken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1159_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T04:01:46-08:00","id":15289,"title":"","content":"Hm, Ghent sound exciting, need to read more on that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1159-kjetilkverndokken","name":"kjetilkverndokken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1159_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T04:05:02-08:00","id":15290,"title":"","content":"&quot;(I were thinking of maybe Africa or Asia, but need to read a bit more up on a few countries before that is going to happen)&quot;<br /> <br /> One of these days I'm going to run a Mummy game set in Kinshasa, which is basically the most dangerous city on this planet.<br /> <br /> I should probably be patriotic and recommend Vienna. Eh.<br /> I like Eastern European cities, particularly the more corrupt and less safe ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T04:11:16-08:00","id":15291,"title":"","content":"Paris - Vienna... those to are very much cities I could want to have games in. never used them before either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1159-kjetilkverndokken","name":"kjetilkverndokken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1159_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T04:34:59-08:00","id":15300,"title":"","content":"I ran a Lucifuge game set in Vienna (and surrounding environs) once, and with the right photos as visual aid, the atmosphere it can create is quite distinct.<br /> <br /> EDIT: My reason for suggesting Ghent is that when I were there, I caught the distinct impression of being in an odd time bubble. The city was clean and modern, but rather than having subverted the olden architecture like wild metallic vines like in Copenhagen, it had created a sort of timeless symbiosis with old and new. And I think this sense of timelessness, in spite of growth and modernization, is thematic for Mummy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":508,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/508-sikker","user":"sikker","date":". 11-21-2013, 07:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/508-sikker","name":"sikker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T06:00:23-08:00","id":15324,"title":"","content":"I might connect those three cities together somehow.","signature":"","